5.In any case, since the signatures are now been compared, this Court is of the view that the further retention of the documents is not required for the purpose of the trial and hence, the trial Court is directed to return the documents to the petitioner on the following conditions;
(1) The petitioner shall not alienate any of the properties covered under the documents, without permission from the learned Magistrate;
(2) The petitioner shall execute a bond for a sum of Rs.5,00,000/- (Rupees Five Lakhs only) with two sureties, each for a like sum to the satisfaction of the Judicial Magistrate-II, Chengalpattu.

